+
+	// UpstreamLease names the request that may spend ConnectorData, an upstream
+	// refresh token every client of the user shares, until it expires
+	// (Deckhouse). A provider that rotates refresh tokens accepts each one once,
+	// so its spending is serialized across requests and replicas. The memory and
+	// Kubernetes storages keep it; the SQL, ent and etcd storages do not, and the
+	// spending of the credential is not serialized with them.
+	UpstreamLease UpstreamLease
